```

### The yield-stress side algebra

Yield stress has its own small algebra and gets imported into viscosity:

```rust
/// A yield-stress law: σ_y(p, c). Produces stresses, not viscosities.
pub trait YieldLaw: Send + Sync {
    fn evaluate<S>(&self, state: &PointState<S>) -> Q![pressure];
    fn dependencies(&self) -> Dependencies;
}

pub struct DruckerPrager {
    pub cohesion: Q![pressure],
    pub friction_angle: Q![dimensionless], // in radians
}

impl YieldLaw for DruckerPrager {
