```

### Source terms

Sources have additive composition over channels, with each channel having its own sub-structure:

```rust
pub enum SourceTerm {
    /// No sources.
    Zero,

    /// Radiogenic heating: per-component constants, mass-weighted.
    Radiogenic { per_component_rate: Vec<Q![heat_source_rate]> },

    /// Shear heating: H = 2 η ε̇:ε̇. Reads viscosity from the dataflow graph.
    /// This is why SourceTerm doesn't implement a free-standing `evaluate`
    /// taking only PointState — it needs upstream sub-model outputs.
    Shear,

    /// Adiabatic heating: H = T α (u · ∇p). Reads α from EOS and needs
    /// extra-state inputs (velocity, pressure gradient) from the framework.
    Adiabatic,

    /// Sum of source channels. Identity: Zero.
    Sum(Vec<SourceTerm>),
}
```

Note the asymmetry: `Radiogenic` carries its own data and is self-contained; `Shear` and `Adiabatic` are *markers* that say "look up this quantity from the dataflow graph." This is the inter-sub-model dependency made explicit.

## Layer 5: The dataflow graph and the constitutive model

Now we tie it all together at the level of the whole model.

```rust
/// A complete constitutive model: the four sub-model trees plus the
/// declared dependencies between them.
pub struct ConstitutiveModel {
    pub eos: EosTerm,
    pub thermal_conductivity: ThermalConductivityTerm,  // not shown; structurally similar to EOS
    pub viscosity: ViscosityTerm,
    pub sources: SourceTerm,
}

/// All the outputs of the constitutive model at a point.
/// These are what the conservation-law solvers consume.
pub struct ConstitutiveOutputs {
    pub eos: EosOutputs,
    pub viscosity: Q![viscosity],
    pub thermal_conductivity: Q![thermal_conductivity],
    pub heat_source: Q![heat_source_rate],
    pub reactions: ComposField,  // reaction rates per compositional field
}

/// Auxiliary inputs from the simulator that aren't part of the local
/// PointState — needed by some source terms (shear heating reads η; adiabatic
/// reads u and ∇p).
pub struct AuxInputs {
    pub velocity: Q![velocity],
    pub pressure_gradient: Q![pressure_per_length],
}

impl ConstitutiveModel {
    /// Evaluate the whole graph at a point, in topological order.
    pub fn evaluate<S>(&self, state: &PointState<S>, aux: &AuxInputs)
        -> ConstitutiveOutputs
    {
        let eos = self.eos.evaluate(state.pressure, state.temperature, &state.composition);
        let viscosity = self.viscosity.evaluate(state);
        let thermal_conductivity = self.thermal_conductivity.evaluate(state);
        let heat_source = self.evaluate_sources(state, aux, &eos, viscosity);
        let reactions = ComposField::zero();  // not modeled in this example

        ConstitutiveOutputs { eos, viscosity, thermal_conductivity, heat_source, reactions }
    }

    fn evaluate_sources<S>(&self, state: &PointState<S>, aux: &AuxInputs,
                            eos: &EosOutputs, viscosity: Q![viscosity])
        -> Q![heat_source_rate]
    {
